        "original_id": "4edb2e29-ba8f-5949-8dc9-71b14d8f5613",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Grand Hyatt New York, Grand Central Terminal, Midtown Manhattan, New York City\n- People: Donald Trump\n- Roles: President of the United States\n- Events: Commodore Hotel opening, Grand Hyatt renovation\n\nFacts:\n- The building now known as the Grand Hyatt New York originally opened on January 28, 1919, as The Commodore Hotel.\n- In 1980, Donald Trump modernized the exterior and renovated the interior of the Grand Hyatt New York building as his first construction project in Manhattan.\n- Donald Trump was born on June 14, 1946.\n- Donald Trump became the 45th President of the United States on January 20, 2017.\n- The Grand Hyatt New York is a hotel located directly east of Grand Central Terminal in Midtown Manhattan, New York City.",
